311 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (1. What is the CIA triad?)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
312 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Answer: The CIA triad stands for Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability. Confidentiality ensures that information is accessible only to those authorized to have access. Integrity ensures that the data is accurate and reliable, and has not been tampered with. Availability ensures that information is accessible to authorized users when needed.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
313 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Tip: When answering, relate the CIA triad to real-world scenarios, such as protecting customer data, ensuring accurate financial records, and maintaining system uptime.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
314 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 779 0 R
/ActualText (2. What is defense-in-depth? What does a 'layered' approach to security  mean?)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
315 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Answer: Defense-in-depth is a security strategy that uses multiple layers of defense to protect information. This approach ensures that if one layer fails, others will still provide protection. Examples include firewalls, intrusion detection systems, encryption, and employee training.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
316 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Tip: Highlight how this strategy is similar to a castle with multiple defenses: moat, walls, guards, etc. Emphasize its importance in modern cybersecurity.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
317 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (3. What's the difference between hashing, encoding, and encryption?)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
318 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Answer: Hashing converts data into a fixed-length string of characters, which is typically a digest that represents the data. It is irreversible. Encoding transforms data into a different format using a scheme that is publicly available, meant for preserving data usability. Encryption transforms data into a different format to protect it, and it can be reversed with a key.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
319 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Tip: Use examples like hashing passwords, encoding URLs, and encrypting emails to clarify your answer.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
